CHALLENGE 1: THE INVENTORY RACE (The 'synchronized' keyword)
================================================================================
SCENARIO: An e-commerce site has 10 items in stock. 100 customers try to
buy 1 item each at the exact same millisecond. Without safety, you'll
sell more items than you have (overselling).

1. Create a class 'Warehouse'.
2. Add 'private int stock = 10;'.
3. Create a method 'public void fulfillOrder()'.
   - If stock > 0, decrement stock and print "Order filled".
   - Else, print "Out of stock".
4. IN MAIN:
   - Start 100 threads that all call 'warehouse.fulfillOrder()'.
5. PROBLEM: Notice you'll see more than 10 "Order filled" messages.
6. FIX: Add 'synchronized' to the method and observe the fix.

